The metered VM is the cleanest part of the [-kernel-]{+kernel. Its design is kept,+} and [-stays in design: prepaid instructions, exact resumption after-]{+its code is re-derived for the new opcodes (§9). Four properties make up that design. Every instruction is paid for from+} a [-cutoff, exact ledgers, and results-]{+work budget before it runs. A run+} that {+is cut off when its budget is spent can be resumed exactly where it stopped. The ledgers of work spent are exact. And the results+} are identical however [-the-]{+a+} run is [-sliced. So does the-]{+cut into slices. The+} rule that every finished program is verified at the [-root-]{+root,+} on every [-row.-]{+row, is kept as well.+}
