"Shipped" means load-bearing in widely used systems. "Replicated" means several independent working implementations. The literature reports carry a verification tag on every figure, and the citations. Most figures below were checked against the source online. These were not: the 17-year span for OpenCog (from memory; its benchmark claim was checked against an abstract); FlashMeta's deployment and the identity of e-graphs, version-space algebras, and tree automata (abstracts only); anti-unification as a product (a summary only; the paper could not be fetched). {+The auditors also declared three gaps. Three of four sub-searches on 2025–26 work ran out of quota, so "none found" for learned inverses and learned termination guards is a weak negative. Some figures exist only in plots. All line-count estimates for minimal implementations are the auditors' own.+}
